window.docContents[80].resolve({"/Terms-and-Sorts/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Terms-and-Sorts--Typed-Terms":{"contents":"A cvc5 term.\n\nTyped terms have a type parameter for the actual cvc5-sort of that term. For basic sorts like\nboolean and integers, cvc.lean relies on the obvious builtin lean types.\n\nA boolean literal.\n\nBinary conjunction.\n\nAn integer literal.\n\nSome term operators are polymorphic however, addition for instance works on any arithmetic terms as\nlong as they have the same sort.\n\nBinary addition.\n\nNotice the\n\nA cvc5 term.\n\nAs their path implies, untyped terms are just terms\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level CVC5 API\u0009Terms and Sorts","header":"2.1. Typed Terms","id":"/Terms-and-Sorts/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-CVC5-API--Terms-and-Sorts--Typed-Terms"}});